1
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:05,100
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(New bonus scenes)

2
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:07,420
(Pre-discussion banter)

3
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:08,190
Yue,

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:09,270
is that your real name?

5
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:10,820
(No stage name here)
Yeah.

6
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:11,740
Is that your real name?

7
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:12,180
(Real name)
Yep.

8
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:12,950
And you?

9
00:00:12,950 --> 00:00:14,320
(Dead serious)
Nope.

10
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:15,590
Then what's yours?

11
00:00:15,910 --> 00:00:17,050
(Everyone's curious)
Ding what?

12
00:00:17,330 --> 00:00:18,150
Ding Chengxin.

13
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:19,110
(Confession time)
That's my real name.

14
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:20,310
All right.

15
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:21,550
We can't use stage names anymore?

16
00:00:21,550 --> 00:00:22,100
Right.

17
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:22,990
Not at all?

18
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,830
I think we still can.

19
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:26,550
For variety shows, at least.

20
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:28,150
I'm not sure about variety shows.

21
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:29,230
I think you have to put your name.

22
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:29,990
(Real name (stage name))
Your real name first,

23
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,030
then your stage name in parentheses?

24
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:31,670
Yeah.

25
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:33,550
So it's basically the same as before.

26
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:34,870
All right, close the door.

27
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:35,350
Come on.

28
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:36,770
Close it.

29
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:40,280
(This feels familiar)
Why does this feel like my bit?

30
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:43,430
(Detective takes charge)
Everyone, grab your script

31
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:47,510
and follow me
into the back room to discuss.

32
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:49,230
You grabbed these for us earlier, right?

33
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:49,710
Nope.

34
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:50,520
(Let me act this out)

35
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:51,420
What does that mean?

36
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:54,480
I'm not holding back today.

37
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:56,230
Where do you guys want to sit?

38
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:57,040
Anywhere's fine.

39
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:57,840
(Don't mind us)
Sit wherever.

40
00:00:57,840 --> 00:00:58,640
Put these here first.

41
00:00:58,650 --> 00:00:59,510
These two.

42
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:00,870
(Digging into the clues)
Put them down. We'll go one by one.

43
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:02,190
Come on, Ding.

44
00:01:02,750 --> 00:01:03,400
Come in.

45
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:06,540
(What's the secret
behind the strawberry mark?)

46
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:08,230
You said earlier you'd seen

47
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:10,430
my body,

48
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:12,310
and there was a silver mark, right?

49
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:14,630
(Absolutely sure)
Yeah. I'm sure it was you.

50
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,190
(Sincere)
But I don't have any wounds.

51
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,510
Right, he has no wounds.

52
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:19,100
All I have is...

53
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:20,340
(Curious)

54
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:21,380
(Puzzled)

55
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:23,980
A strawberry mark.

56
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:26,940
(Curious)

57
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:29,240
(Can't hold it in)
A strawberry mark?

58
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:31,110
Why is there a strawberry mark?

59
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:31,930
No idea.

60
00:01:31,930 --> 00:01:33,210
(So many questions)
Why a strawberry?

61
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:35,150
(Ke has a theory)
Then it's pretty obvious.

62
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:38,110
When Ning Waver died,

63
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:40,510
he was face-to-face

64
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:41,380
with the Lord of Tui City,

65
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:42,690
so a sword stabbed
through his right chest

66
00:01:42,690 --> 00:01:43,920
would pierce the other's left chest.

67
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:45,580
(Agrees)
Right.

68
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:48,230
Not necessarily.

69
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:50,710
Why do you keep shooting it down?

70
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:53,030
(Hear me out)
That's just one possibility.

71
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:55,030
It could be true,

72
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:57,390
but you can't call it a fact.

73
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:59,470
Right.
They could've each been stabbed once.

74
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:01,670
Why can't we call it a fact?

75
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:03,030
Because he went to the scene,

76
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,230
saw your body,

77
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:06,070
and checked your wounds.

78
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,390
It's just that after you woke up,

79
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,870
the wound was gone.

80
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:10,270
So how can you be so sure?

81
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:11,510
Because isn't that already established?

82
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:12,790
That's what he said.

83
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:14,030
First of all,

84
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:15,270
there's nothing wrong with his account.

85
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:16,790
(Looking closely)
This is weird.

86
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:19,390
First,
Ning Waver was already unconscious.

87
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:21,030
No one knows what happened

88
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:21,750
in this room after that.

89
00:02:22,330 --> 00:02:22,840
Right.

90
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:24,510
So you can't conclude

91
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:27,270
that one sword
went through both of them.

92
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:28,470
Okay.

93
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:31,020
(Seriously analyzing the hidden weapon)

94
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:33,230
But she's the biggest outlier.

95
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:35,310
I think she's too clean.

96
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:36,580
(Where did that come from?)

97
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:37,870
Being clean isn't that weird.

98
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:39,270
She's a guest, after all.

99
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:40,500
(Seriously, Ning?)

100
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:44,790
(Just kidding)
I'm kidding.

101
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:46,950
There's one thing about her
that's really strange.

102
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:49,470
Go on.

103
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:53,110
She never mentioned
that she knows martial arts.

104
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:55,820
I forgot to mention it.

105
00:02:55,820 --> 00:02:56,460
(Oh?)

106
00:02:56,580 --> 00:02:58,020
(Is it really that simple?)

107
00:02:58,060 --> 00:02:59,580
(Or is there more to it?)

108
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:00,670
When I was five,

109
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:02,110
I was adopted.

110
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:03,190
Then when I was ten,

111
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:04,910
my adoptive mother passed away.

112
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:05,320
(Serious)

113
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:07,910
My adoptive father raised me on his own

114
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:10,870
and taught me some martial arts,

115
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:12,990
including the Corn Blossom Needle.

116
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:14,950
Corn Blossom Needle?

117
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:16,270
Did he teach you how to use

118
00:03:16,270 --> 00:03:17,410
(Popcorn Needle)
the Popcorn Needle?

119
00:03:17,540 --> 00:03:18,740
(Ning, you must be hungry)

120
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:19,760
Popcorn?

121
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,190
Corn Blossom Needle.

122
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:24,230
So it's a hidden weapon?

123
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:25,310
Right, a hidden weapon.

124
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:26,110
That's the key clue.

125
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:27,230
(Yang Glory's skill: hidden weapons)
She uses hidden weapons, right?

126
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:28,590
That's her specialty.

127
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:31,110
What about the blueberry picking?

128
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,870
(Picking)
Just picking blueberries.

129
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:34,110
That's pure farm work.

130
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:35,230
(Picking nonstop)
All handwork.

131
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:36,510
Basically, she's an artisan.

132
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:39,550
Among everyone here,

133
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:44,990
I look like the best fighter, don't I?

134
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,990
I'm the only one who uses two swords.

135
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:48,700
(Sword)

136
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,180
But I think

137
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:52,460
killing those two

138
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:54,120
may have nothing to do
with martial arts skill.

139
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,390
Because of that bottle of medicine.

140
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:57,870
With that medicine,

141
00:03:57,880 --> 00:03:59,470
even an ordinary person could do it.

142
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:02,420
(I'm deep in detective mode)

143
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:04,820
(Turns out everyone's just acting brave)

144
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:05,780
(He Ha and Ning Waver)

145
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:06,620
(go help Ding Pillar and Ke Stubborn)

146
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:07,520
Wait!

147
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:09,090
(Don't leave us!)
Ning!

148
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:10,270
What?

149
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:11,190
(Trembling)
Once the cage closes, you're good.

150
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:12,070
No, I'm scared.

151
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,350
(Anything for you)
Okay, I'll stay with you.

152
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:16,390
(Tiny question)
Jin, you're more scared than I thought.

153
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:17,270
(Trying to play it cool)
No, I...

154
00:04:17,270 --> 00:04:18,310
I'm just scared of the dark.

155
00:04:18,310 --> 00:04:19,300
Everything else is fine.

156
00:04:19,380 --> 00:04:20,820
(Then who's this?)

157
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:22,070
Yang's pretty brave.

158
00:04:22,080 --> 00:04:23,710
I thought she'd be scared.

159
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:27,590
But Yuwen and Qian...

160
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:29,150
Are they really that scared?

161
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,350
Yeah, they can't handle it.

162
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:33,020
You'll hear them screaming
all over the place.

163
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:33,900
(Dungeon 1: The Battle of the Heirs,
Aah!)

164
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:34,780
(Dungeon 2:
Undercover in a Scam Factory)

165
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:36,020
(Truthfully)
I'm scared too.

166
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:36,610
I'm really scared.

167
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:38,020
You actually are?

168
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:38,960
(Scared stiff)
Yeah, I totally froze.

169
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:40,060
Ning, are you scared?

170
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:41,010
Very.

171
00:04:41,010 --> 00:04:42,250
So, Ning is a scaredy-cat too?

172
00:04:42,250 --> 00:04:45,730
But he's the kind who's scared
and still tries to...

173
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:48,240
act tough.

174
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:49,680
He pretends he's not scared.

175
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:52,150
But under that robe,

176
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:53,390
his legs are shaking.

177
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:55,270
My upper body looks all composed,

178
00:04:55,280 --> 00:04:56,350
while my legs are trembling.

179
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:57,740
(Turns out everyone's acting brave)
Oh.

180
00:04:57,780 --> 00:04:59,900
(Today's clue-hunting hype squad)

181
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:02,390
Why does he have a sleep patch on?

182
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:03,750
He doesn't sleep well.

183
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:04,510
See? There's no way

184
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:06,110
(Detective, clear my name!)
my weapon did that.

185
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:08,150
Could be.

186
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:09,470
(Just minding my own business)
That wound is huge.

187
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:10,510
(Fate keeps picking on me)
Mine's tiny.

188
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:12,670
No, he already said
it was the Qide Sword.

189
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:13,360
Yang Glory,

190
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:14,410
put on your glove

191
00:05:14,410 --> 00:05:16,050
(As you wish, my pretty sis)
before you touch the body.

192
00:05:16,050 --> 00:05:17,090
Just wear one.

193
00:05:17,090 --> 00:05:17,930
He can't get it on.

194
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:18,670
(Thoughtful Ke online!)
Just put on one.

195
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:20,550
Here, I'll help you.

196
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:21,630
(Thanks, bro)
Thanks, Zhou.

197
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:23,150
I'll put it on for you, cutie.

198
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,000
Come on, Zhou.

199
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,680
(He stays focused on the case)
You four...

200
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:28,510
I think the two of us are good guys.

201
00:05:28,860 --> 00:05:29,800
I think so too.

202
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:31,440
For today,

203
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:32,790
let's play it up a little.

204
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:34,360
(Play it up)
Give it a little...

205
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:34,680
Yeah.

206
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:36,390
Make it more fun.

207
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:37,950
(Period-drama mode)
More of a period-drama vibe.

208
00:05:37,950 --> 00:05:38,910
Okay.

209
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:39,710
Should we loosen up a little?

210
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:41,750
(These two get me)
Yeah, give it some flair. Make it fun.

211
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:44,390
You don't have to go as far as I do.

212
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:45,750
I can't go that far.

213
00:05:47,020 --> 00:05:49,220
(Checking around)

214
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:51,230
Why are you taking his shoe off?

215
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:52,310
Wait!

216
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:56,150
Isn't this my key piece of evidence?

217
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:58,630
(Made in Shanghai)
Shanghai. I'm from Shanghai.

218
00:06:03,060 --> 00:06:03,900
=The Truth (Season 4)=

219
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:05,120
(SVIP updates Wed & Thu at 12PM.)

220
00:06:05,130 --> 00:06:06,180
(VIP updates next day at 12PM,
one week early.)
